      "html": "<p>Since the very first start of breeding sports in ornamental fish, some strains were named after the town where they first appeared. Examples are the \"Vienna Emerald Guppy\", the \"Hamburg Swordtail\" or the \"Bristol Shubunkin\".</p><p>This tradition also took place in dwarf shrimps, and so a \"Cologne strain\" of Caridina logemanni exists. Specimens from that strain exhibit an extraordinarily high degree of red coloration.</p>"
    }
